				</ukm:Metadata><Primary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1977/42/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1977/42/body" NumberOfProvisions="144" RestrictStartDate="2026-10-05"><Part DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1977/42/part/I" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1977/42/part/I" NumberOfProvisions="27" id="part-I" RestrictStartDate="2026-10-05"><Number>Part I</Number><Title> Preliminary</Title><Pblock DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1977/42/part/I/crossheading/protected-and-statutory-tenancies" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1977/42/part/I/crossheading/protected-and-statutory-tenancies" NumberOfProvisions="3" id="part-I-crossheading-protected-and-statutory-tenancies" RestrictStartDate="2023-05-18"><Title> Protected and statutory tenancies</Title><P1group><Title> Protected tenants and tenancies.</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1977/42/section/1" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1977/42/section/1" id="section-1"><Pnumber>1</Pnumber><P1para><Text>Subject to this Part of this Act, a tenancy under which a dwelling-house (which may be a house or part of a house) is let as a separate dwelling is a protected tenancy for the purposes of this Act.</Text></P1para><P1para><Text>Any reference in this Act to a protected tenant shall be construed accordingly.</Text></P1para></P1></P1group></Pblock></Part></Body></Primary></Legislation>